# phi-agent — A1 (assistant) perimeter (phios-agente.md §4.3, revised by
# phios-agente-delta.md §3.1).
#
# Recomputed per active project: no other project is visible (§4.3). The
# active project name comes from PHI_AGENT_PROJECT; when it is unset the
# @PROJECT@ lines below expand to an empty path and are skipped, so the
# container still starts for the V-01..V-04 proof without a project selected.
#
# Ordering: the writable XDG bind comes first; every memoria.md is then
# re-bound read-only over it. memoria.md at ALL THREE levels (system,
# personality, project — delta D-01) stays read-only: the agent CANNOT write
# its own memory, and that is enforced by these mounts, not by the interface
# (§8.4, ADR 094). Only `phi agent memory accept` (the client, outside the
# containment) promotes a proposte/ file into a memoria.md.
#
# Two things are done in phi-agent-contain, not here, because the .paths
# grammar has no globs or lists: (a) re-binding each personalita/<name>/
# proposte/ writable, (b) the read-only folders of interest from
# <project>/folders.list (delta D-02).

# A1's own XDG trees — writable (§4.3 "albero XDG di A1: scrittura").
# opencode keeps its sessions, auth and cache here.
rw   @AGENT_DATA@                @CONTAINER_HOME@/.local/share
rw   @AGENT_STATE@               @CONTAINER_HOME@/.local/state
rw   @AGENT_CACHE@               @CONTAINER_HOME@/.cache

# System memory — read-only (delta D-01). Written only by
# `phi agent memory accept --level system`. "?" so a machine that has never
# run `phi agent init` still starts for the V-01..V-04 proof.
ro?  @AGENT_DATA@/memoria.md     @CONTAINER_HOME@/.local/share/memoria.md

# The engine config, read-only. A single file, not the whole .config dir.
# "?" — you create it from opencode.example.json (it carries the model id).
ro?  @AGENT_CONFIG@/opencode/opencode.json   @CONTAINER_HOME@/.config/opencode/opencode.json

# Personalities — read-only (§4.3). "personalita/ scrive solo l'utente"; the
# agent never writes here. This re-binds the SAME container path (already
# exposed writable via @AGENT_DATA@ above) read-only. phi-agent-contain then
# re-binds each <name>/proposte/ writable underneath.
ro?  @AGENT_DATA@/personalita    @CONTAINER_HOME@/.local/share/personalita

# The active project. Everything read-only except the two write areas.
ro?  @PROJECT@                   @CONTAINER_HOME@/project
ro?  @PROJECT@/memoria.md        @CONTAINER_HOME@/project/memoria.md
rw?  @PROJECT@/proposte          @CONTAINER_HOME@/project/proposte
rw?  @PROJECT@/output            @CONTAINER_HOME@/project/output
